## What this PR adds

`.vibeguard.yml` — your settings:

```yaml
live_probe: false            # allow harmless HEAD row-count proofs on your own API
public_on_scoreboard: false  # show this repo's name on the public scoreboard
```

Both default to off. Change them any time; the next scan picks them up.

## What VibeGuard never does

- It never reads your data — probes are HEAD requests that return only a row count.
- It never uses a secret/service_role key it finds. It reports them instead.
- It never touches repos you didn't install it on.
- It never opens a guessed fix — if a safe fix needs a decision, you get an issue with options.

Merge this to start receiving fix PRs, or close it to opt out (the bot stays installed but quiet).
